  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5344",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have a direct target relationship with AN3-CA through multiple pathways. The first pathway links Mollicellin N to A704, which is then targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and finally, 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid targets AN3-CA. The second and third pathways similarly connect Mollicellin N to A704 and then to 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which also targets AN3-CA. These pathways suggest that Mollicellin N may act through a series of intermediate molecules that ultimately lead to the activation of AN3-CA. The shared involvement of A704 and 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid in multiple pathways supports a potential mechanism involving molecular signaling or metabolic pathways. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N may influence AN3-CA via a complex network of targets, potentially through a cascade of molecular interactions that are not fully elucidated.",
